course the new ultra wide  camera gives you a really cool  perspective that you simply can't get on  the iPad air and the best part of all is  that you can shoot 4k 60fps video with  either of the pro s cameras compared to  only 1080  p 30fps video with the air now for the  front-facing selfie cam  they're both seven megapixels but since  the iPad pro has face ID  you also get portrait mode so the  selfies look much more appealing Apple  also updated the microphones on the  20/20 Pro so here's a comparison between  the two this is a microphone quality  tests on the 2019 iPad air this is a  microphone quality test on the 2020 iPad  pro now moving on to the new lidar  scanner on the pro it basically improves  depth sensing and tracking and work  similarly to how face ID does here's a  clip from AI fondo showing the lidar  scanner in action it projects a ton of  dots and then scans them to detect depth  we tested out an augmented reality app  on both of these iPads and you can  clearly see that the iPad pro is giving  us much more accurate depth and distance  tracking compared to the air which  doesn't have the lidar scanner now this  feature isn't a very big deal right now  but if you're planning on keeping your  iPad for a couple of years keep this in  mind since augmented reality apps could  become extremely popular a huge plus for  the iPad pro is that it's the only iPad  that features Wi-Fi 6 compared to slower  Wi-Fi 5 on the air now getting into  performance the pro gets the new a 12 z  chip which has a slight improvement over  the a 12 X while the air gets the  regular a 12 chip one major difference  is that the pro now gets six gigabytes  of RAM compared to only three on the air  so multitasking and using productivity  apps is going to be better on the pro  and geek bench 5 the pro scored a much  higher score in terms of multi-core  performance and in the metal graphics  test the pro scored over twice as high  as the air which is useful for things  like gaming rendering and augmented  reality the more realistic antutu test  also shows us a pretty good improvement  for the pro especially in terms of the  RAM performance the great thing about  being in 2020 is that a lot of apps have  been optimized to take advantage of the  iPad pros  formants for example you can now play  fortnight at 120fps on the iPad pro  compared to only 60 fps on the air and  there are a whole lot more games that  support 120 fps so gamers should  definitely go for the pro and even in  basic navigation the pro is gonna feel  more snappy because of the combination  of extra performance double the RAM and  the 120 Hertz refresh rate display that  makes everything feel super smooth  especially using the Apple pencil and  the quad speaker setup is also a  difference you'll feel every day  maybe even more so than promotion now  does this mean that the iPad air is bad  or that it's slow absolutely not  it's still one of the best tablets out  there and it easily beats a lot of  Android tablets but the pro is just a  big step above one huge benefit for the  iPad pro is that it's the only iPad that  supports Apple's upcoming magic keyboard  case which is going to be released in  May and it's extremely unique since it  makes the iPad float it packs the  awesome new magic Keys directly from the  16 inch macbook pro and it also features  a trackpad this is going to be great to  use with iPad OS 13.4 s new cursors  support which basically allows the iPad  to finally be a laptop replacement now  if you're interested in how to use  cursive support check out that video  after this one's over  now a big plus for the new air is that  there are going to be keyboard cases  with track pads coming soon like the  Logitech combo touch which is already on  Apple's website and yes it also features  a trackpad and it's only a hundred and  fifty dollars compared to the Apple  magic keyboard case which is three  hundred dollars but the magic keyboard  case has one more huge advantage  pass-through charging this means that  you can charge your iPad through the USB  C port on the keyboard case itself which  leaves the original USB C port free to  use for things like transferring files  or connecting to a display the iPad air  gets a lightning port that can't do that  and it doesn't supply as much power so  it's not as easy to transfer files from  a variety of devices and honestly I  think the magic keyboard case will be a  huge hit even at the $300 price because  of the brand new floating iPad design so  with all of that said and  paired which iPad is the better value  well it really depends on what you want  to do with it if you just want an iPad  for regular tasks like browsing the web  using common apps and streaming Netflix  then the iPad air is one of the best  tablets you can buy but if you want to  play games the pro is a much better  option if you want great multitasking  performance or you want to do some video  or photo editing get the pro if you want  the best Apple pencil experience and  performance get the pro if you want the  snappiest and most fluid display the pro  gets a 120 Hertz display if you really  care about how the speaker sound then  definitely get the pro if you'd like to  transfer and store files on the iPad the  pro will be much more convenient and if  you want to use the best keyboard case  ever made then you have to get the pro  but if all of those things aren't that  big of a deal to you and you'd much  rather save your cash then I'm sure  you'll be very satisfied with the iPad  air since it packs enough performance to  take care of most of the common tasks  that people need it to do so hopefully  you guys enjoy this comparison video  make sure to tap the like button and  click the circle above to subscribe for  more videos like this one thanks for  watching and we'll see you in the next  video  [Music]
 

